Use case: ui-mockup. Create realistic, production-quality UI design for Gyro's existing macOS coding-agent working-process component.
User correction: eliminate the nonminimal designs. Strictly minimal, compact, native-feeling, typography-led. This is a new design proposal grounded in the attached references. Image1 (current Gyro screenshot) grounds product identity only; image2 (prior flattened work rail) grounds row vocabulary only. Neither is a target to copy wholesale. Use only the scene specified below. Do not import unrelated screenshot text, approval cards or full app navigation.
Target dimensions: 1200 x 800 landscape. Render ONE focused cropped chat excerpt at natural760px content-column width with realistic14–16px UI typography. Scale the excerpt uniformly if needed to fit; never stretch. Place content around the middle with natural margins; no huge dead areas, no giant poster typography, no decorative title or branding footer. Output one design, not a board of multiple ideas or multiple time states.
ACTUAL Gyro system: uniform graphite #1c1c1c background; text #ededed, secondary #b5b5b5, faint #a0a0a0; hairlines white5.5% when needed. Native system sans/SF for text, SFMono/Menlo for code. Typical14px body,13px work,12px metadata; compact26–30px work rows at intended scale. 4px restrained control corners. Blue #60b0ff only if focus/action needs it; no gratuitous color. Completed work neutral. No large cards, no cards inside cards, no surface tint around whole run, no shadow, no bevel, no gradient, no texture, no glow, no chips around paths, no repeated checkmark+activity-icon pairs, no emoji, no avatar, no status legend, no persistent marketing heading.
Keep necessary information, do not achieve minimalism by hiding pending approvals or failures. This chosen frame is an ordinary live run: no approval pending, no failure, no end result yet.
Shared illustrative content for fair comparison across allthree choices:
- user message "Bound the sync queue retries." as a quiet right-aligned unboxed line;
- one small neutral header "Working for 42s" and an accessible-looking small stop square at far right as the only action button;
- narration "I’ve added the retry limit. I’m checking the failure case.";
- recorded history includes "Read src/sync.ts", "Read src/sync.test.ts", "Edited src/sync.ts" with illustrative measured diff "+18 −4";
- current activity "Running tests" with exact command "pnpm test", only one tiny neutral live spinner, no success checkmark on active work;
- no test output claiming passed because the test is running.
No dates, costs, token totals, progress percentages or remaining-time predictions. Provide exact readable text with correct spaces. Use spacing/grouping first, optional one hairline only if essential. This is the hero working-process component; leave all other app UI offscreen.
